Answer: Because the JVM determines which overridden method to execute at runtime based on the actual object being referred to. For example:

```java
Payment payment = new UPI();
payment.pay(1000);
```

Although the reference type is Payment, the UPI implementation executes.

Answer: Because the payment amount can change for every transaction. Passing it as a parameter allows the same payment method to process different amounts. Example:

```java
payment(1000);
payment(2500);
payment(5000);
```

